  "file_classes": ["singleModel"],
  "frame_title": "Self-crossing Eulerian circuit (same graph as figure8_tour, wrong transition)",
  "frame_description": "Identical two-square figure-eight graph, but vertex 0 is paired (e0,e4) and (e3,e7) -- opposite edges, whose chords interleave in the ccw order [e4,e7,e0,e3]. Still a valid, edge-disjoint, Eulerian-complete circuit, but NOT crossing-free: it is the non-A-trail counterexample RQ2 is about. Contrast with figure8_tour.fold.",
